\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Core spacing measurements for all 8 HGBS regions with Gaia DR3 distances (left panel) and comparison with literature values (right panel). \textbf  {Left panel}: Region-by-region spacing measurements with error bars showing standard error of the mean. From left to right: Taurus (0.198 pc), Ophiuchus (0.206 pc), TMC1 (0.195 pc), CRA (0.248 pc), Perseus (0.248 pc), Serpens (0.331 pc), Orion B (0.313 pc), Aquila (0.346 pc). Horizontal reference lines: red dashed = weighted mean (0.279 pc), green dotted = 3D-corrected value (0.35 pc), grey dash-dotted = IM92 theoretical prediction (0.4 pc). \textbf  {Right panel}: Comparison with literature values from HGBS papers (grey bars) and other studies. Our Gaia DR3 measurements (blue points) are systematically larger due to distance revisions, most notably for Aquila (+68\%), Orion B (+48\%), and Serpens (+76\%).}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spacing}{{1}{5}{Core spacing measurements for all 8 HGBS regions with Gaia DR3 distances (left panel) and comparison with literature values (right panel). \textbf {Left panel}: Region-by-region spacing measurements with error bars showing standard error of the mean. From left to right: Taurus (0.198 pc), Ophiuchus (0.206 pc), TMC1 (0.195 pc), CRA (0.248 pc), Perseus (0.248 pc), Serpens (0.331 pc), Orion B (0.313 pc), Aquila (0.346 pc). Horizontal reference lines: red dashed = weighted mean (0.279 pc), green dotted = 3D-corrected value (0.35 pc), grey dash-dotted = IM92 theoretical prediction (0.4 pc). \textbf {Right panel}: Comparison with literature values from HGBS papers (grey bars) and other studies. Our Gaia DR3 measurements (blue points) are systematically larger due to distance revisions, most notably for Aquila (+68\%), Orion B (+48\%), and Serpens (+76\%)}{figure.1}{}}
